            <p>After Ashura, when this oppressed caravan of captives set off, the enemies raised the heads of the martyrs on spears. The white-bearded head of Hazrat Habib (AS) was also on a spear. On the way to Kufa, Habib's (AS) young son Qasim came; he went to the wretched man who had his father's head and cried, saying: "For God's sake, take as much wealth as you want from me, take whatever reward you want, but give me the head of my old father." But that cruel man did not give the head.</p>
            
