    "content": "\n        <div style=\"font-family: 'Arial', 'Helvetica', sans-serif; font-size: 1.1em; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; direction: ltr;\">\n             <p><strong>Gilgit-Baltistan's Electoral Battle 2026: End of Outdated Traditions and the Rising Sun of New Leadership</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Written by: Haji Shabbir Ahmad Shigri</strong></p>\n\n            <p>\nIt is said that when the earth calls, ideas are born, and when problems exceed limits, revolution knocks. At this time, the paradise-like region of Gilgit-Baltistan in northern Pakistan stands at such a historical turning point. The 2026 general elections in Gilgit-Baltistan are not just about transfer of power, but an open declaration of war against this outdated, traditional, and hereditary politics that has deprived this devout and patriotic people of their fundamental rights for decades.\nThe most pleasant and beautiful aspect of this electoral contest is that this time, the conscious youth class, educated people, and sincere social personalities of Gilgit-Baltistan are coming forward as independent candidates, free from the clutches of hereditary parties. These new faces are a fresh breeze in the region's politics, who have come forward with a public manifesto and the true call of the earth instead of drawing-room politics.\nIn Skardu city, problems are growing under the shadow of beauty. If we talk about Skardu city, the heart of Baltistan, tourists from all over the world come to see its beauty, but the suffering its residents are going through is a blot on the calendar. The city's roads are in a state of disrepair, which not only severely affects local movement but also deals a blow to tourism.\nDuring the winter season, when the temperature drops below zero, Skardu city does not even get to see electricity for many days. In the bitter cold, darkness and a freezing climate have become the fate of the people here.\nThe serious issue of clean drinking water (abnushi), backward transport system, and lack of medicines and modern machinery in hospitals have made the lives of citizens miserable.\nThe tyranny of air fares: 40-minute journey and a 50,000 rupee ticket! On one hand, Gilgit-Baltistan has not yet been given full provincial status, and on the other hand, the worst economic burden in the form of air fares has been placed on the poor people and tourists here. In neighboring countries, where international flight tickets start from 30 to 35 thousand rupees, here a one-way fare for just a 40-minute flight to Skardu, a part of Pakistan's own territory, is being collected from 40 thousand, 45 thousand, and sometimes up to 50 thousand rupees!\nPreviously, only the national airline (PIA) had its way, but now other private airlines have also started dipping their hands in this flowing Ganges and are making hay. There is no concession for local patients, students, and poor local people, nor for tourists. This is sheer oppression and economic exploitation of the people of Gilgit-Baltistan, for which the silence of the ruling circles is criminal.\nGBA 7, Skardu 1: Muhammad Ilyas—The New Ray of Hope:\nAgainst these same darknesses and public deprivations, an extremely dynamic, lively, and sincere young leader, Muhammad Ilyas, has entered the field as an independent candidate from Skardu's constituency GBA 7 (Skardu 1). Unlike traditional politicians, Muhammad Ilyas does not believe in rhetoric; instead, he has come up with such a revolutionary and practical manifesto for the 2026 elections that has the ability to change Skardu's destiny.\nMuhammad Ilyas' 21-point manifesto is not just a collection of promises but a scientific and practical solution to each of Skardu's problems:\nEnd of energy crisis: To end electricity, his first priority is to get approval by removing the flaws in small hydro projects on the Hargisa Nala with modern machinery and the 5-megawatt project that has been stuck for 15 years above the Sadpara village.\nElimination of rights infringement in solar power: To raise a strong voice against the reduction of Skardu's share in the 100-megawatt solar project approved by the federation to just 6 megawatts, and to implement the master plan of Skardu city that has been stuck for the last 5 years is part of his agenda.\nModern drinking water and environment: Providing clean water through modern filtration plants and water lifting on the Hargisa Nala and river, and upgrading the Phaliong Water Diversion Project so that water is not wasted.\nRevolution in health and education: Ensuring the appointment of at least one medical doctor in every dispensary in Skardu, bringing medicines to hospitals, and personally supervising the training of teachers on modern lines and educational institutions is his resolve.\nConstitutional rights and National Finance Commission (NFC): Fighting for Gilgit-Baltistan's share in the NFC award on the basis of area and backwardness, and making progress on a new social contract with the Federation of Pakistan on constitutional matters is the strongest and most far-reaching point of his manifesto.\nInter-sectarian harmony: Remaining always ready for the promotion of love and mutual brotherhood among sects on Skardu's soil is Muhammad Ilyas' fundamental principle.\nThe decision is now in the hands of the people!\nDevout residents of Gilgit-Baltistan and especially Skardu! For the past many years, flatterers and hereditary politicians who make verbal collections will stand before you with their hands folded. But remember, if today we do not support educated, capable, and sincere young independent candidates like Muhammad Ilyas, then our future generations will also continue to burn in the same agony of electricity, water, roads, and expensive flights.\nElections 2026 is the day to change Skardu's destiny. Now the time has come that we shatter the idols of hereditary politics and, on the basis of \"manifesto and character\", make sincere young people like Muhammad Ilyas successful and enter Skardu into a new era of development.\nSupport Muhammad Ilyas in changing the destiny of the region and make him successful by voting for the scooter election symbol.\n\n</p>\n            <br>\n            <div style=\"display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 20px; justify-content: center; align-items: stretch; margin: 20px 0;\">\n                {/* Zamana News */}\n                <div style=\"flex: 1 1 300px; max-width: 500px; text-align: center;\">\n                    <img\n                        src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/dlafcjt6z/image/upload/v1780464290/GB_Election_zamana_news_2026-06-03_brhvth.jpg\"\n                        alt=\"Zamana News Newspaper Clipping\"\n                        style=\"width: 100%; height: auto; border-radius: 12px; box-shadow: 0 4px 15px rgba(0,0,0,0.15);\"\n                    />\n                </div>\n\n                {/* Daily Yome-e-Takbeer */}\n                <div style=\"flex: 1 1 300px; max-width: 500px; text-align: center;\">\n                    <img\n                        src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/dlafcjt6z/image/upload/v1780464289/GB_Election_daily_yome_e_Takbeer_2026-06-03.jpeg_uobdsv.jpg\"\n                        alt=\"Daily Yome-e-Takbeer Newspaper Clipping\"\n                        style=\"width: 100%; height: auto; border-radius: 12px; box-shadow: 0 4px 15px rgba(0,0,0,0.15);\"\n                    />\n                </div>\n            </div>\n        </div>\n        "
